title: NetBird: Network Routing Peers
agents: netbird
catalog: cloud/netbird
license: GPLv3
distribution: cmk-netbird (community)

item:
 The name of the NetBird network.

description:
 This check monitors the routing peers of one NetBird network.

 Only enabled routers count. A router that is bound to peer groups is resolved to
 the peers in these groups, and a peer that appears more than once counts once.

 The service is {OK} if all routing peers are online, {WARN} if at least one is
 online and at least one is offline, and {CRIT} if no routing peer is online
 (also for a network with a single router) or if the network has no routing peer.
 The text lists the offline peers with the age of their last_seen value and
 points out peers with an expired login as a likely cause.

 The version of the routing peers is compared with a reference version. NetBird is
 at 0.x, so the minor version counts: the same minor with another patch level is {OK},
 one minor version behind is {WARN} (default), three or more behind is {CRIT}
 (default), a lower major version is {CRIT} (default). Peers with a newer version
 than the reference are {OK}. Versions that cannot be parsed (empty,
 "development") never cause an alert; the text names such peers. The reference
 version can be the latest GitHub release, a fixed version or the highest peer
 version; the text shows which one is used. The state of the service is the
 maximum of availability and version state.

 Metrics: number of routing peers online and in total.

discovery:
 One service is created per network with at least one enabled router.
